          "const": "unvoiced-model-envelope-v1"
        },
        "strength": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 1
        },
        "max_attenuation_db": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 12
        }
      },
      "description": "Optional bounded model log-gain envelope for noise excitation in explicitly unvoiced stop and affricate regions. Native C0 only. Preserves the existing run calibration from an unchanged excitation reference; does not move release timing or renormalize the candidate. Omit to disable; either numeric control at zero bypasses exactly. Independent of score.synthesis and its seed semantics. Cannot coexist with legacy gain_mode relative. Filter memory can affect adjacent samples, so the noise-envelope bound is not a pointwise output-waveform bound."
    },
